   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The passato prossimo",
     "texto": [
      "It's formed with the present of **avere** (**ho, hai, ha, abbiamo, avete, hanno**) plus the **past participle**: **Ieri ho parlato con Sara** (yesterday I spoke to Sara). It corresponds to both the English present perfect («I have spoken») and the simple past («I spoke»).",
      "Watch out! **Ho** also means «I have» (**ho fame**, I'm hungry), but before a past participle it works as a tense auxiliary."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Forming regular past participles",
     "texto": [
      "**-are → -ato** (parlare → parlato), **-ere → -uto** (ricevere → ricevuto), **-ire → -ito** (dormire → dormito, capire → capito).",
      "With the auxiliary «avere», the past participle generally ends in **-o** and doesn't change with the subject: **Io ho parlato, noi abbiamo parlato**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
